  "reviewFindings": [
    "The Gen1 runtime exports retain synchronous module loading. Event invocation resolves the project through GoogleAuth only if absent, shares concurrent discovery, retries failed discovery without inventing a project, and then invokes the complete Firebase SDK wrapper. Descriptor copying preserves discovery metadata and .run.",
    "Direct regression tests use the real installed Firebase SDK wrapper and synchronous require path; they cover configured project, absent project, concurrent calls and first-discovery failure. The deployed Node 22 runtime must still be checked by CI/cloud validation.",
    "Development readiness uses existing short-lived delegation followed by one GET of derived paperRegisterState/v1. Missing, incomplete or mismatched state skips promotion; authentication/transport failures remain errors. No backfill or source-data write occurs in this check.",
    "Main production promotion still depends on successful protected backend verification. Non-main hosting cannot proceed when readiness is false. Shared backend post-checks execute only after a successful hosting promotion.",
    "Deployment no longer attempts the reserved GCLOUD_PROJECT configuration. The final runtime adapter replaces that rejected proposal; successful local tests do not establish that the live publishing fault has been repaired."
  ],
